      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to use the tangent addition formula. The formula for the tangent of a sum of two angles is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\n\nIn this problem, we are given that \\( \\tan x = 2 \\). We are asked to find \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\).\n\nUsing the tangent addition formula with \\(a = x\\) and \\(b = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\tan x = 2\\) and \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this calculation using Python.\n```python\n# Given value\r\ntan_x = 2\r\n\r\n# Value of tan(pi/4)\r\ntan_pi_over_4 = 1\r\n\r\n# Calculating tan(x + pi/4)\r\ntan_x_plus_pi_over_4 = (tan_x + tan_pi_over_4) / (1 - tan_x * tan_pi_over_4)\r\nprint(tan_x_plus_pi_over_4)\n```\n```output\n-3.0\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).",
